IMPORT `int-tests-fixtures`

-- int-tests-red: properties that follow from the Law's own words and that the nine readings taken do NOT deliver together.  Every assertion in this file states what the Law says and is meant to FAIL today;
-- each failure is a seam between two groups' modules, not a mistake in the integration layer, and each is listed in NOTES.md under "Defects found in group modules".  The positive controls at the end are the
-- same questions asked on the reading under which the groups agree: they must be satisfied, which shows that the failing assertions fail on the readings and not on a typing mistake.
-- Seam 1 (IP35, the unit of a term of imprisonment): the Law says "2 years".  Asked on 2 October 2026, a term of 2 years ends on 2 October 2028, which is 731 days later because 2028 has a 29 February.
--   The maximum of "2 years" must therefore admit a term of 731 days beginning on 2 October 2026, whatever unit a model uses.  On the days unit the four groups that read it (G6 Article 20(6); G7 Articles 21(9) and 23(7);
--   G8 Articles 26(10) and 29(1); G9 Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)) refuse it: G6, G7 and G8 take 2 years as 730 days, and G9's cap converts the stored 24 months to days FROM the start day (731) and compares with 730.
--   Four assertions fail for this one cause.
-- Seam 2 (IP29): Article 11(2)(e)(ii) asks for a draft statement of intentions "if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies".  An Order under Article 13(9) that requires only the details of payments in the
--   annual return (limb (a)) is not an Order under 13(9)(b).  Group G5 offers one Boolean for all three limbs; used for the question Article 11(2)(e)(ii) asks, it answers TRUE.  One assertion fails.
-- Seam 3 ("a registered charity"): the Law's definition (Article 1) needs an entity entered in the general or the restricted section.  Group G1 reads it so (an NPO body corporate is not an entity in the text of
--   12 April 2023, so it cannot be a registered charity); group G8 (Article 26(2)) reads the standing alone, and says the same body is a registered charity.  One assertion fails.

§ `Integration layer -- seams that fail on the readings taken`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with the days unit` MEANS `Int the readings of the fleet` `the calendar year` `days`

GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`24 months and a fine` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 24, fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

§§ `Seam 1 -- IP35: a term of 2 years beginning on 2 October 2026 is 731 days; on the days unit it is outside the maximum of "2 years" in every group that reads the unit`

-- Expected by the Law: a term of exactly 2 years is within a maximum of 2 years.  Fails: G6.
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
-- Fails: G7.
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2026 10 2) ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
-- Fails: G8.
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
-- Fails: G9 (the cap reads the 24 months stored in the penalty, converts them from the start day, and compares with 730).
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` ((`the readings with the days unit`)'s `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2026 10 2)

§§ `Seam 2 -- IP29: an Order that requires only payment details (limb (a)) is not an Order under Article 13(9)(b)`

GIVETH A `Order under Article 13(9)`
`an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS TRUE, `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE, `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE
-- Expected by the Law: the answer to "does an Order under Article 13(9)(b) apply?" is the same whichever group is asked.  Fails: G5's composite fact is TRUE, the limb-specific fact (the one the integration layer wires) is FALSE.
#ASSERT `Int IP29 the composite fact of group G5` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY EQUALS `Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`) EMPTY

§§ `Seam 3 -- "a registered charity": group G1 needs an entity within Article 2(1); group G8 (Article 26(2)) reads the standing alone`

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the NPO body corporate entered in the general section` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Les Amis du Jardin"
        standing IS `entered in the general section`
        purposes IS (`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes
        facts IS `Int fx an NPO body corporate`
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "M. Du Feu")
GIVETH AN Entity
`that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 12 April 2023` MEANS
    `Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 12 April 2023` EMPTY (YMD 2025 10 15) `the NPO body corporate entered in the general section`
GIVETH A `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26`
`the NPO body corporate itself as the person addressed` MEANS
    `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26` WITH `capacity of the person under Article 26(2)` IS `the entity itself`, `standing of the entity on the register` IS `entered in the general section`, `the entity was formerly a registered charity` IS FALSE, `governor while the entity was registered` IS FALSE
-- Expected by the Law: whether an entity is a registered charity is one question with one answer.  Fails: G1 says no, G8 says yes.
#ASSERT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` `that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the NPO body corporate itself as the person addressed`

§§ `Positive controls -- the same questions on the readings under which the groups agree (all must be satisfied)`

-- Calendar months: a term of 2 years from 2 October 2026 is 731 days; all four groups accept it.
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2026 10 2) ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` (YMD 2026 10 2) 731
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` ((fleet)'s `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2026 10 2)
-- IP29: an Order whose limb (b) is TRUE is an Order under Article 13(9)(b) on both facts.
GIVETH A `Order under Article 13(9)`
`an Order that requires a statement of intentions` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS FALSE, `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS TRUE, `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Int IP29 the composite fact of group G5` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires a statement of intentions`) EMPTY EQUALS `Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` fleet (JUST `an Order that requires a statement of intentions`) EMPTY
-- "A registered charity": for the same body in the text of 16 October 2025 (which has sub-paragraph (ba)) G1 and G8 agree.
GIVETH AN Entity
`that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 16 October 2025` MEANS
    `Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 16 October 2025` EMPTY (YMD 2025 10 16) `the NPO body corporate entered in the general section`
#ASSERT `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` `that body as Article 2 leaves it in the text of 16 October 2025` EQUALS `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) `the NPO body corporate itself as the person addressed`
